# Test Failure Triage

> **DRAFT** — sections marked `TODO` must be completed by the system-tests team.

Apply this rule when a user asks to triage a failing test (e.g. "triage this failure", "this test failed on the nightly, handle it").
The input is usually a test name, a CI job URL, or a Test Optimization link.

The key question is to determine the root cause. Runs on this CI uses the last release of all components. So the root cause is unlikely a tested components. The outcome of the process is bases on the most probable culprit.

The procedure has four steps. **Never create a ticket or a PR without an explicit confirmation from the user** (see [Confirmation](#confirmation)).

## Possible culprits

* A component has been released, and a test was activated only for the release version of this components, and so, it was never tested
* A test is flaky because anything in the test logic is flaky
* A test is flaky because anything in a tested component is flaky
* 

